{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for f254698d07598666a2e329474024a97c5f0ac8b5, tree 1f06506d5391b54fe8dacf300b8e4d9bd4163dd8. One blocking finding after the complete review.\n\nF1 (P1) — Fund the foreign source of a provisional scope's confirmation. packages/derive/src/reserve.ts:134 initializes the provisional task with entry(1), which carries one entryBytes of bytes. The actual confirmation judge in packages/derive/src/delivery.ts records useOf(from, source); packages/scope/src/delivery.ts:266 retains those foreign source bytes with the confirmation. That retained input is additional to the confirmation's own journal bytes. The shared reservation therefore omits a reachable producer and can admit a birth whose already owed confirmation cannot fit at the filled byte ceiling.\n\nIndependent reproduction: bc3ee4dee818d39f7a6a02b7716ce0cb68d6372b includes the complete scratch script. Real in-memory genesis, creator-result and child-confirmation judges/folds, explicit fixture authority, followed by ByteUsage/capacityFull; this is not a native SQLite or provider run. With entryBytes=4096, all earlier entries fit (1078, 2342, 2629 bytes). The valid creator result is 3510 bytes and the confirmation is 1194; each separately fits. Before confirmation the child reserves 8192 bytes (confirmation plus closing checkpoint), afterwards 4096. Retaining the source and confirmation consumes 4704 bytes, so Used+Reserved increases by 608 over a ceiling that admitted the provisional state at equality; capacityFull names scopeBytes. A second valid source of 3910 gives 1008 excess. The production post-fold check consequently retries that owed confirmation at this ceiling. No forced record, fabricated entry, size-cache change or false historical text size is involved.\n\nRepair the provisional task in the existing shared Amount traversal to include its accepted foreign-entry writer maximum while preserving its one-entry count and all omitted-capacity behavior. Keep runtime and Replay on that same term. Add a meaningful native two-scope regression: admit the provisional birth at Used+Reserved equality, produce a valid sufficiently large creator result, evict, record its confirmation, retain the source once, and show the closing checkpoint remains funded. Check the one-byte-under birth refusal and rollback, Replay agreement and legacy behavior. Update the note/inventory to name this producer. This is a reservation correction, not a settlement ceiling exemption.\n\nCoverage: primary a64c227c read FIRST and in full (216 lines); all 107 changed paths and their current exact-head bindings exhausted in six batches, none stale or retired. Reviewed contract/client changes, the shared graph and arithmetic, originating request and actual item/holder settlement bookkeeping, native owner/pin quotations, creation closure/body rules, SQL counting/transaction/restart behavior, Replay conditional refusals/alias recovery and transitive coverage retraction, metrics and changed tests. The two exported lanes correctly refuse the unbounded hold/check ancestry snapshot; catalog inventory makes no activation claim. C1 remains the adopted entry-slot floor under acdd/63195, not an invented full handoff guarantee.\n\nArchitecture: the one reservation graph and post-fold transaction boundary fit the adopted design; F1 prevents complete funded settlement. Security: no separate authority or disclosure defect found; bounded producer refusal, canonical domain/digest identities and explicit historical byte gaps remain required. Simplification: correct the existing provisional term; no second mechanism is needed.\n\nImplementation-note fidelity: faithful about logical units, producer refusals, C1, legacy omission and proof limits, but its complete whole-scope guarantee is not yet established because of F1. Gate33e30708 explicitly supersedes the note's pre-freeze unresolved-gate sentence. Tests do not lie: raw bookkeeping/calculator and synthetic authority/provider boundaries are identified; native storage/eviction/HTTP replay cases meaningfully exercise their stated invariants. They miss confirmation retention at a filled byte budget.\n\nVerification: independently read and verified all three finitely granted gate files (size, SHA256, stable regular-file identity). Exact-head terminal gate passed: Vitest329 files/1668 cases, with one skipped file/three skipped cases; Node25 and Counting55 passed. The RefcountedCanceler cross-DO diagnostic points into Vitest abort/timeout handling; actor/cause remain unassigned and the pass establishes no harness stability fix. Scripted resets and the retention-trigger fault match explicit fixture code; they do not explain away that warning. Four HTTP Content-Type warnings remain. Earlier4c's terminated test run remains failed/incomplete, not part of a combined pass. Broader1d3/833 and R4 physical measurements/provider behavior remain open.\n\nChecker scratch read-only builds reproduce both generated asset modules byte-exact; Counting's three disk payloads, MIME types and digest comments also agree. Whitespace check passed and the project checkout stayed clean. No package install, source/ref mutation, gate repeat, push or deployment by checker.\n\nCurrent-Main carry: independently rebuilt the Git tree hashes from leaves, validating base/source/Main hashes first. Main df806 adds exactly144 disjoint reviewed paths relative to95959; overlap with the107 capacity paths is zero. Combining them yields 2014 leaves and b68082624ca86f0bd9af4da22954e61a74ff4526, preserving boundary blob2b70982682798ccbd962bda55a6b1d3f32d63679 and all reviewed card files. This carry introduces no additional finding, but does not authorize landing this rejected capacity head. Return a repaired frozen Source and its new-head gate evidence for review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a64c227c51c253e8c10c811244e8c1bb0a2ad12c","binding":"assigned","head":"f254698d07598666a2e329474024a97c5